%N A122678 Invariant number of polygons of n-circum-C_5 H_5 systems.
%C A122678 Note that the index in Eq. (5) of the paper by Brunvoll, Cyvin and Cyvin must be 2k-1, not 2k as published, to reproduce the numbers. - _R. J. Mathar_, Nov 23 2014
%H A122678 Colin Barker, <a href="/A122678/b122678.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A122678 Jon Brunvoll, Sven J. Cyvín, and Bjørg N. Cyvín, <a href="https://match.pmf.kg.ac.rs/electronic_versions/Match34/match34_91-108.pdf">Azulenoids</a>, Match 34 (1996), 91-108.
%H A122678 Klée Pollock, Jonathan D. Kroth, Jonathon Riddell, and Thomas Iadecola, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.23716">Group word dynamics from local random matrix Hamiltonians and beyond</a>, arXiv:2510.23716 [cond-mat.stat-mech], 2025. See Fig. 18, row L=5.
%H A122678 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (4,-4,1).
%F A122678 a(n) = 5*Fibonacci(2*n-1)-4 = A106729(n-1)-4.
%F A122678 G.f.: -x*(1+x)^2 / ( (x-1)*(x^2-3*x+1) ). - _R. J. Mathar_, Nov 23 2014
%F A122678 From _Colin Barker_, Nov 03 2016: (Start)
%F A122678 a(n) = 2^(-1-n)*(-2^(3+n)-(-5+sqrt(5))*(3+sqrt(5))^n+(3-sqrt(5))^n*(5+sqrt(5))).
%F A122678 a(n) = 4*a(n-1)-4*a(n-2)+a(n-3) for n>3. (End)
%F A122678 E.g.f.: exp(3*x/2)*(5*cosh(sqrt(5)*x/2) - sqrt(5)*sinh(sqrt(5)*x/2)) - 1 - 4*exp(x). - _Stefano Spezia_, Jul 31 2026
%t A122678 5*Fibonacci[2*Range[30] - 1] - 4 (* _Paolo Xausa_, Jul 31 2026 *)
%o A122678 (PARI) Vec(-x*(1+x)^2/((x-1)*(x^2-3*x+1)) + O(x^40)) \\ _Colin Barker_, Nov 03 2016
